Global correctness: allocation-history-lower-violation (run 1).
The first sale removes the minimum feasible basis and tightens the next sale’s
lower bound. The second sale’s 20 USD basis is then impossible despite a
balanced final history.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight unrealized-gains --to 2024-02-28 --format json <<'LEDGER'
commodity USD
  format 1,000.00 USD
  default
commodity FUND
  format 1,000.000 FUND
account Assets:Bank
account Assets:Broker
account Income:CapitalGains

P 2024-01-01 FUND 4 USD

2024-01-01 Buy cheap units
  Assets:Broker  10 FUND {{10 USD}}
  Assets:Bank  -10 USD

2024-01-02 Buy middle units
  Assets:Broker  10 FUND {{20 USD}}
  Assets:Bank  -20 USD

2024-01-03 Buy expensive units
  Assets:Broker  10 FUND {{30 USD}}
  Assets:Bank  -30 USD

2024-02-01 First sale
  Assets:Broker  -11 FUND {{12 USD}} @@ 44 USD
  Assets:Bank  44 USD
  Income:CapitalGains  -32 USD

2024-03-01 Impossible second sale
  Assets:Broker  -10 FUND {{20 USD}} @@ 40 USD
  Assets:Bank  40 USD
  Income:CapitalGains  -20 USD

2024-04-01 Close the booked remainder
  Assets:Broker  -9 FUND {{28 USD}} @@ 36 USD
  Assets:Bank  36 USD
  Income:CapitalGains  -8 USD
LEDGER

